From f27cf860b72eccf93ec96a00578e81cfd57021f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Mostovoy <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:40:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 22/22] hw/arm/mt7981: front panel LEDs

Machine options led1..led32 describe the board's LEDs:
"<name>: <colour> <source> [+ <colour> <source>...]", several colours
of one lamp joined with "+".  Sources: gpio:N[:low] (SoC GPIO),
phy:ADDR:N (LED pin of the Ethernet PHY at an MDIO address, from its LED
registers: RTL8221B 0xd032.. / 0xd040 / 0xd044, GPY211 PHY_LED and
VSPEC1_LED), ws2812:BUS:N (a WS2812B chain on a SPI bus, decoded from the
leds-ws2812b bit stream) and pwm:N (PWM controller channel, enable bit and
duty).  Every 50 ms the sources are sampled; several level changes within
200 ms count as blinking.  "led-state" (qom-get /machine) returns the
states for the launcher's LED panel, gpio-log=on prints the changes.

Works on MT7981, MT7986 and MT7987 (PWM channel blocks per SoC).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
